    "updated_at": "2023-05-08T15:06:24Z",
    "body": "What is the proposed commit message?\r\n\r\nI have two thoughts here:\r\n* Privileging the top-level module script is weird. It would make more sense to match CSS where each style sheet stands on its own and can impact the fetches it ends up causing.\r\n* Even though non-JavaScript module scripts don't have descendants, we should not lump this logic together with JavaScript and instead have it be generic so it can be shared with future module scripts that do have descendants (e.g., Wasm).",
