    "created_at": "2023-06-22T19:34:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-22T19:38:55Z",
    "body": "As for mutability of script fetch options: tl;dr I'm mostly neutral (very slightly preferring the non-mutable way though), with random thoughts below.\r\n\r\nOne one hand, I like the non-mutability of script fetch options because:\r\n\r\n- We can plumb script fetch options without checking where it is already used (currently it is safe to be modified at the timing the current PR describes, but this needed checking every script fetch options references, as in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9210#pullrequestreview-1413230811),\r\n- We can centralize the mutations (?) only at its construction, e.g. we would \"update\" the script fetch options from the referencing script to its descendants at [descendant script fetch options](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#descendant-script-fetch-options), including its referrer policy among with others.\r\n- Making things not changing over time has been important (especially in implementation), e.g. to disambiguate whether something is the state at the time of script preparation, load completion, and script evaluation. So using the same data member for both \"refererrer policy that is used to load the script itself\" and \"referrer policy that is used to load the descendant script\" depending on when/where it is used is alarming.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, I also agree with https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9210#issue-1682091177, i.e. non-mutable version might be not super better (e.g. we need to add a new parameter to [descendant script fetch options](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#descendant-script-fetch-options) and a new member to concept-script which might complicate the spec than needed), so I feel the current PR and Chromium impl CL are also OK.\r\n\r\n(But this might be because I'm not really strictly careful about referrer policy -- if I should be really careful e.g. like nonce and CSP, I'd take the non-mutable path, distinguishing \"script's fetch options's referrer policy\" used for the script itself and  \"script's response referrer policy\" to be used for descendants -- I'm not sure it's worth distinguishing these two with extra care)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
